sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — MorphoEval overall 70.1/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py` (overall 70.1/100, down from 92.8 in v2). The remediation added a genuinely solved Mitchison (1980) canalization model on a growing hexagonal cell lattice (three cell-division stages, conductance inheritance, 16 measurements, 12 self-test checks, 3 new Lean 4 theorems) and a solved Sachs incision bypass with an alpha = 0 control. It reproduces the spatiotemporal order of vein formation in the weak sense that 77-81 % of newly canalized cells lie inside pre-existing intercostal panels and that vein order is stage-ordered, but it does NOT close loops (beta_1 = 0, specimen 1843 areoles), its solved network is a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands rather than a pinnate midrib with secondaries, its emergent S_vein/S_par (0.67) disagrees with the value v2 prescribed (0.31), and its strand angles (26.8 +- 14.2 deg) miss the specimen (52.9 deg). Building the solver exposed that the Pass 2 \"simulations\" of lamina drainage, wound bypass and Feugier topologies are analytic profiles, constants and hand-drawn graphs tuned to the script's own reference JSON; these are now labelled PRESCRIBED / GRAPH TEMPLATE in `measure_morphoeval()` but remain in the figure and the measurement set, and the v2 CLI flags are parsed but unused. Rendering is deterministic and SHA-pinned. Overall 70.1/100 (faithfulness 64.3, reproducibility 83.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_comparison.png: rendered output of 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py at d58a084, image/png, 1339843 B, 2700×1680 px, artifact_sha256 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381 (sha256 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381), spec_fingerprint c7349d3e4102c9f6306702949c507eeadd9b480c0de0ed099e56fb40eb8cea36. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c7349d3e4102c9f6306702949c507eeadd9b480c0de0ed099e56fb40eb8cea36; artifact_sha256: 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json=55e0f743ada83918..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/growing_lamina_reference.json=a51f3d788874ecb6..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg=7f67774708f8e952..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations.bib=95f1b35cf42a8ae7..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations_pass3.bib=b3a22b5ca5439009..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/scout_manifest.json=94a1d6a85fe649c5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109: facilitated-diffusion canalization dD_ij/dt = alpha |phi_ij|^p + beta - gamma D_ij with phi_ij = D_ij (S_i - S_j); linear feedback gives diffuse flow, quadratic feedback gives winner-take-all 1-cell strands whose auxin concentration drops below the parenchyma (S_vein < S_par) | Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 & Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262: polar auxin transport canalization and C-shaped vascular bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision | Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375: PIN1 carrier-allocation dynamics, open trees vs closed areoles; Feugier & Iwasa (2006) 243:235-244: canalization alone does not close loops | Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20:1015-1027 & Kang & Dengler (2004) Int. J. Plant Sci. 165:231-242: higher-order veins form progressively inside areoles bounded by lower-order veins; reconstructed_in_script: SOLVED (Pass 3): Mitchison (1980) facilitated-diffusion canalization with soft-saturating feedback alpha |phi|^2/(1+phi^2/phi_s^2) on a hexagonal cell lattice that divides 12x11 -> 24x22 -> 48x44 (75 -> 312 -> 1281 cells) with conductance inheritance; vein cells 7 -> 29 -> 155, nesting of new strands inside pre-existing panels 0.81 / 0.77, S_vein/S_par = 0.67 (emergent), sink intake / production 0.98, beta_1 = 0 at every stage (also 0 with the irreversible-differentiation ablation) | SOLVED (Pass 3): Sachs (1981) transverse incision on a 20x16 hex stem with a pre-established strand: sink intake 0.991 (incised, canalizing) vs 0.609 (alpha = 0 NPA control) vs 0.988 (intact), 6-cell lateral deflection; hop-count path ratio L_wounded/L_intact = 1.00 (metric insensitive to lateral deflection) | PRESCRIBED (Pass 2, retained and now labelled): 2-pathway exponent sweep p in {0.5, 1.0, 1.4, 2.0, 2.5} (the p = 1.4 point uses a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766), analytic 12-column and 18x14 D/S profiles with hard-coded dip ratios (0.3105 / 0.6895), a Gaussian Sachs bypass centreline with constants 0.9852 / 0.0804, and two hand-drawn Feugier venation graphs (V=16/E=15 -> beta_1 = 0; V=28/E=41 -> beta_1 = 14) | Automated segmentation of the SHA-256-pinned cleared dicot leaf (primary midrib, secondary angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg, 1843 closed areoles, vein areal coverage 0.416); transfer_boundary: Hexagonal cellular lattice with isotropic 2x refinement stands in for a growing leaf blade; strand orientations are quantised to ~30/60/90 deg so the branch-angle comparison with the specimen (52.9 deg) is lattice-limited | Facilitated diffusion (Mitchison 1980) is solved; polar PIN1 carrier allocation (Mitchison 1981 / Feugier 2005) is only verified algebraically (Law 3) and the hand-drawn graphs are not its output | Reference values 1.38 / 0.985 / 0.08 (Sachs) and the exponent-regime table in the pinned reference JSON are not digitised from any figure; they are carried as qualitative benchmarks; does_not_claim: Loop closure / areole formation or quaternary areole subdivision (beta_1 = 0 in every solved configuration; the specimen has 1843 areoles) | A finite-element or measured growth field; 3D mechanical blade expansion; polar PIN1 dynamics on a growing domain." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:1235-1243 and 1100-1119 — sachs_dynamic_bypass_relative_tortuosity is a hop count that returns 1.00 for a 6-cell deflection. Use Euclidean segment lengths between hex-cell centres along the Dijkstra path and compare against the 1.38 benchmark only after that benchmark is either digitised from Sachs (1981) or dropped.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:1868-1871 — CLI flags --alpha, --beta, --gamma, --exponent-p are parsed but never used (also true in v2, which credited them). Wire them into the solver (or remove them) and render a parameter sweep (alpha, phi_s, D_diff factor) showing strand count, nesting fraction and vein density per stage, with >= 3 seeds for uncertainty.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:243-254, 338-357, 446-461 — docstrings of the three prescribed functions still say \"Simulate\"; rename or re-document them as `prescribe_*` / `template_*` so code traceability matches the measurement labels.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:243-335 and 150-198 — the 18x14 lamina fields and the 12-column profiles are analytic Gaussians with hard-coded dip ratios 0.3105 / 0.6895 (L195, L295) and a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766 at p = 1.4 (L158). Replace them with the hex solver run at each exponent p (the engine already takes exponent_p) so the bifurcation curve and S_vein/S_par are solved, and drop the fitted constants; reconcile the solved 0.67 with the prescribed 0.31.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:446-548 — `simulate_feugier_venation_topologies` types in V/E/C (L493, L523) and the measurements feugier_*_betti1_loops (L1303-1318) still count a drawing as a result. Either implement the Feugier et al. (2005) polar carrier-allocation ODEs on the hex engine (the prototype's circulating-vortex failure must be diagnosed: fix the refinement inheritance of polarity as a vector and add auxin degradation inside veins) and derive beta_1 from the solution, or delete the template measurements.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:720-730 and 1274-1282 — the solved network is a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands (angles 26.8 +- 14.2 deg, hex axes at 30 deg) rather than a pinnate midrib with ~53 deg secondaries. Run the solver on a second lattice (square with diagonals, or random Voronoi cells) and report the lattice sensitivity of the strand angles and of the vein-order map before comparing with the specimen.",
            "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:950-1034 — loop closure is absent (beta_1 = 0, specimen 1843 areoles). Implement one published loop mechanism and test it: Feugier & Iwasa (2006) auxin production inside veins with bidirectional flux, or Runions et al. (2005) margin convergence points connecting to two veins; measure nested areole subdivision per stage against the specimen's areole-area distribution (areas already available from segment_leaf_venation_specimen, L620-640).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json:46-115 — the Sachs (1.38 / 0.985 / 0.08) and exponent-regime \"_ref\" values have no figure or table provenance. Digitise the relevant Mitchison (1980) Fig. 1-2 curves (or state that no quantitative benchmark exists) and version the JSON (dataset_id v2) rather than carrying the Pass 1 constants as references." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.701"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 034 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

